# Simple CSS Selectors

- Prefer the simplest selector that works: one class (`.content-block`, `.block-body`).
- Never use `data-testid` in CSS — those attributes are for tests only.
- Do not nest ancestor chains unless required to override or scope.
- To override an existing rule, extend the base with one specific qualifier only when necessary (`.block-body` → `.layout-sidebar-left .block-body`).
- Avoid overcomplicated stacks like `.block-grid-layout [data-testid="…"] .block-body`.
